  </div>
  <div class="dg-legend"><span><i></i>AWS API call</span><span><i class="pull"></i>agent reads and reports</span><span><i class="tn"></i>tailnet</span><span><i class="ts"></i>tailnet link</span><span><i class="out"></i>outbound from an agent</span><span><i class="blk"></i>inbound, dropped</span></div>
  <div class="dg-steps">
    {/* design.md §2 (no hermetic server), §4.7 (init builds the foundation), §6.2 Create */}
    <div><b>1</b><h4>Manage</h4><p>The app or CLI calls your AWS account directly. It builds the fleet's foundation once, then launches each agent on its own machine.</p></div>
    {/* design.md §6.3 First boot, §2 (heartbeat to DynamoDB) */}
    <div><b>2</b><h4>Boot</h4><p>On each agent, <code>hermeticd</code> pulls its config and secrets from the foundation, installs Hermes and reports health back.</p></div>
    {/* design.md §5.2 (tailnet policy entries: who may reach tag:hermetic, on which ports), §7.2 (Tailscale SSH, Serve) */}
    <div><b>3</b><h4>Reach</h4><p>Agents join your tailnet. Chat, logs, SSH and the agent's desktop travel over it, and a tailnet policy rule decides who may connect.</p></div>
    {/* design.md §7.2 (no inbound SG rules, nftables host firewall; Tailscale connects outbound), §1 */}
    <div><b>4</b><h4>Stay sealed</h4><p>Agents have no inbound ports. Nothing on the internet can open a connection to one, while the agent can still reach the web and model APIs.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
